I've got another use case:

``` ts
var validators = [
    Validators.required,
    invalidNumber,
];
if (!(this.minValue == null || this.maxValue == null))
    validators.push(outOfRange(this.minValue, this.maxValue));
```

The push statement is a type mismatch error and I could fix this by using `var validatiors: ValidatorFn[]` as type annotation.

I'm using this code temporary:

```
import { AbstractControl } from '@angular/common/src/forms-deprecated/model';
import { ValidatorFn } from '@angular/common/src/forms-deprecated/directives/validators';

export class GenericValidator
{
  static required(errorMsg: string): ValidatorFn {
    return (control: AbstractControl): {[key: string]: any;} => {
      var val: string = control.value;
      return (val === '') ?
                 {'required': errorMsg} :
                 null;
    };
  }
}
```

a little example of my validator with a custom error message "coonfigured"
